<title>USA: Porta Systems Q1 sales down, loss vs profit.</title>
<headline>Porta Systems Q1 sales down, loss vs profit.</headline>
<dateline>SYOSSET, N.Y. 1997-05-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>(Dollars in thousands except per share data)</p>
<p>					     Quarter Ended March 31,</p>
<p>						 1997		 1996</p>
<p> Sales				  $   12,480	$   13,221</p>
<p> Gross profit				4,014	     4,338</p>
<p> Total operating expenses		3,738	     4,283</p>
<p> Operating income			    276		  55</p>
<p> Interest expense, net		   (874)	   (2,169)</p>
<p> Other income (expenses)		   135	     (151)</p>
<p>Loss before income taxes,</p>
<p>minority interest and</p>
<p>  extraordinary item		     (463)	   (2,265)</p>
<p> Income tax expense			 (14)		(13)</p>
<p> Minority interest			    75		 110</p>
<p> Loss before extraordinary gain	(402)	   (2,168)</p>
<p>Extraordinary gain on early</p>
<p>  extinguishment of debt		     8	     3,033</p>
<p> Net income (loss)			 (394)		 865</p>
<p>Per share data:</p>
<p>Loss before</p>
<p>  extraordinary items		   (0.06)	    (0.80)</p>
<p> Extraordinary item			 0.00		1.15</p>
<p> Net income (loss) per share	  (0.06)		0.35</p>
<p>Weighted average shares</p>
<p>  outstanding (in thousands)	   6,142	     2,625</p>
<p>NOTES: 1996 net share includes an extraordinary gain of $3,033,000, or $1.15 per share, from the exchange of the company's 6% Subordinated Debentures for convertible non-interest bearing notes and common stock.</p>
<p>Operating income for the quarter 1996 was also hurt by the fiber optics business operations sold during that quarter.</p>
<p>Full company name is Porta Systems Corp.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610))</p>
